>>> Auto after a split parameter list: the colon follows the parenthesis.
class Point {
  Point(this.someVeryLongParameterName, this.anotherVeryLongParameterName, this.third) : first = 1, second = 2;
}
<<<
class Point {
  Point(
    this.someVeryLongParameterName,
    this.anotherVeryLongParameterName,
    this.third,
  ) : first = 1,
      second = 2;
}
>>> (wrap.initializer_lists.colon=new_line) new_line after a split parameter list: an unbroken list stays inline.
